<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trail of Tears</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1830–1850</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Trail of Tears was the forced removal of Native American nations from their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homelands</a> in the south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-territory">Indian Territory</a> west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> under the Indian Removal Act of 1830. The name refers above all to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherokee">Cherokee</a> removal of 1838 and 1839, when US troops drove some 16,000 people west, about 4,000 of whom died. The Choctaw, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, Chickasaw and Seminole suffered similar removals.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trail-of-tears.jpg" alt="Trail of Tears" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Cculber007 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TrailofTearsMemorial-3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
